WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.290
Kaley Cuoco was a seasoned screen veteran
long before she started working as Penny on

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:08.280
The Big Bang Theory, but even she isn't immune
to the odd flub on the set every now and then.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.440
Here's a look at some of the funniest goofs
from a very funny career.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.839
In a ninth season episode of The Big Bang

00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:20.060
Theory, Jim Parsons' Sheldon makes a video
for "Crazy Future Sheldon" and starts the

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.800
explanatory video for himself with some footage
of Penny who, in this outtake, is just way

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.600
too busy with her popcorn to care.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.300
In another take, the camera stays on Sheldon,
who makes a wisecrack about Penny.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.820
Penny and her popcorn, however, aren't having
it.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.740
"If she offers you food, it's safe to take
it.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:44.860
You probably paid for it anyway."

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.940
As the script in this season three episode

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:00.600
was written, Cuoco's Penny reacts to a comment
from Simon Helberg's Howard by sarcastically

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.680
asking, "Are you high?"

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.300
At first, it's co-star Johnny Galecki who
flubs his follow-up line.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.080
"Are you high?"

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.380
"You have a...English."

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.680
The director re-sets the scene and gives instructions
on where to start over, but Cuoco's still

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:17.720
concerned about Galecki.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.380
"Are you high?"

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.620
Still, that's not the end.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.700
"My point is…"

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:27.760
"High!"

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.760
The Big Bang Theory characters hold the Star

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.000
Trek franchise in high esteem throughout the
series.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:42.180
One would think that all of that Star Trek
stuff constantly on the set would have forced

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.880
its way into Kaley Cuoco's brain.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:48.100
But that's clearly not the case, at least
when she's supposed to be giving Spock's famous

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.100
Vulcan salute.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:56.920
"I am Spock…Did I do it wrong?...I did?!

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.360
I've been doing it...Oh, this way."

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.320
In this blooper, Kaley Cuoco stumbles over

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:09.709
a word she probably has to say more than any
other in the line of duty: "Leonard," the

00:02:09.709 --> 00:02:12.580
name of her character's neighbor, then boyfriend,
then husband.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.460
"Leonar...Leonar.."

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.200
"Leonard."

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:16.440
"Balls!"

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.560
Cuoco's blooper then grows infectious, as
co-star Jim Parsons can't get through the

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:24.019
next part of the scene without fudging his
own dialogue.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.100
"...surprisingly, uh, gripping...oh no…"

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:29.540
"Balls.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:30.160
The key word is balls."

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:31.840
"Balls!"

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.599
In the early seasons of The Big Bang Theory,

00:02:36.599 --> 00:02:40.830
Penny makes ends meet waitressing at the Cheesecake
Factory while pursuing her dream of being

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:41.400
an actress.

00:02:42.029 --> 00:02:46.100
To save money, she subsequently exploits her
proximity to the guys by helping herself to

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.720
their food as well as their wifi.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.940
In this fifth season episode, Penny casually
enters the guys' apartment to get the new

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:56.120
wifi password, but doesn't seem to understand
what one actually does with wifi.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:59.279
"Okay, if you can't get me to stop eating
your food, what makes you think you can stop

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.420
me from eating your wifi?"

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.900
The ABC sitcom 8 Simple Rules for Dating My

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:12.740
Teenager Daughter was Kaley Cuoco's first
major role on a successful show.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:17.180
She portrayed the slightly rebellious and
independent daughter of beloved TV icon John

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:17.680
Ritter.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:21.900
The kid versus adult struggle at the center
of the show becomes comically real in this

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.200
blooper from the first season.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:33.820
"Stop imitating me!"

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:34.400
"No!

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:34.920
I was-"
"Stop it!"

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.719
Yes, you can rib Kaley Cuoco on a sitcom set,
but she can give as good as she gets, even

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:43.980
to a legend like John Ritter!

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:48.559
On the set of 8 Simple Rules, Cuoco can't
really start her scene until Ritter walks

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.840
onto the stage and boy is she impatient.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.120
"Ritter!

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:55.260
Action!"

